Stress-corrosion mechanisms in silicate glasses — Ciccotti (@mat-glass-corrosion: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_5MYPVB5E5N1GHFSQ75B046N1QS
Matteo Ciccotti, *Stress-corrosion mechanisms in silicate glasses*, Journal of Physics D: Applied Physics 42 (2009), 214006, 18 pages. [Author's institutional PDF](https://ciccotti.espci.fr/sites/ciccotti.espci.fr/IMG/pdf/Ciccotti2009-JPD-StressCorrosionSilicateGlasses.pdf), [preprint](https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.2809), [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1088/0022-3727/42/21/214006).

Read the entire review, including the competing mechanisms and experimental limitations. Selected crack-growth regimes, humidity/temperature dependence, dissolution/leaching and extrapolation discussion were inspected on 30 October 2026. Similar fits over a narrow observed range can produce very different long-time predictions.

This is free author-hosted access to a copyrighted article; no general adaptation licence was established. Keep figures and manuscripts external. The review supplies research depth alongside the shared brittle-fracture and ceramic sources.

